From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:14:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] backend-drm: match Broadcom SAND modifiers without the column height

A Broadcom SAND buffer carries its column height in the modifier
parameter (fourcc_mod_broadcom_param(), bits 8..55), while the KMS
planes advertise the parameterless DRM_FORMAT_MOD_BROADCOM_SAND128.
drm_fb_compatible_with_plane() compares modifiers exactly, so an NV12
SAND128 buffer from the Raspberry Pi 4 video decoder was never put on an
overlay plane and was composited by GL instead.

When the exact match fails and the modifier belongs to the Broadcom
vendor, try again with fourcc_mod_broadcom_mod(), i.e. without the
parameter.

This is the weston 16.0.0 version; only the surrounding context differs
from the 15.0.0 one.

Related upstream work: the draft merge request
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/weston/-/merge_requests/1640
("backend-drm: Implement DRM_FORMAT_MOD_BROADCOM_SAND128 support"),
marked for testing only.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/fb.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/fb.c
@@ -697,6 +697,14 @@
 
 		if (weston_drm_format_has_modifier(fmt, fb->modifier))
 			return true;
+		/*
+		 * A Broadcom SAND modifier carries the
+		 * column height in bits 8..55 (fourcc_mod_broadcom_param); KMS lists the
+		 * modifier without it, so compare without the parameter.
+		 */
+		if ((fb->modifier >> 56) == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_VENDOR_BROADCOM &&
+		    weston_drm_format_has_modifier(fmt, fourcc_mod_broadcom_mod(fb->modifier)))
+			return true;
 	}
 
 	drm_debug(b, "\t\t\t\t[%s] not assigning paint node %s on %s, "
